## Test Execution in Cursor Web UI

When running tests in Cursor Web UI environments, use the portable test runner script:

```bash
python scripts/run_tests.py tests/test_app_smoke.py -q
```

Or for the full test suite:

```bash
python scripts/run_tests.py -q
```

The test runner automatically handles Python executable detection across different environments (local, Replit, Cursor Web UI, CI/CD).

**Why**: Cursor Web UI may not have `python` in PATH, but the test runner script detects and uses the best available pytest command (`pytest`, `python3 -m pytest`, or `python -m pytest`).

For more details, see `docs/testing/cursor-web-ui.md`.
